Pick the largest logit directly when sampling is greedy.

With temperature 0 the sampler chain ends in the greedy sampler, and no
sampler before it can change which token has the largest logit. Still,
every token built an array of one candidate per vocabulary entry and ran
it through the chain. PLaMo 3 Translate has 107520 entries, so that is
1.3 MB written and then scanned for every token of every sequence.

common_sampler_sample() now scans the logits for the largest value when
the chain can only return that token. The test is conservative: no
grammar, reasoning budget, backend sampling, mirostat, probabilities,
logit bias or suppress tokens, a chain that ends in the greedy sampler,
and before it only samplers that keep the largest logit with the
settings in use. Any other request takes the old path.

The token is the one the chain would pick, except when two tokens share
the largest logit exactly: the scan returns the lower id, and the
chain's order after its partial sort is not specified.

Measured on an RTX 4090 with sixteen slots: the sampler went from
0.19 ms to 0.07 ms per token, and in the extension a long article took
about 6% less time. The translations came out identical.

